From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] phy: allwinner: A733 combo-PHY -- the DP lane map and lane inverts on the real path

Two pieces of board data that were only ever written by test instrumentation
outside this series. Without them, the DP lane map at COMB0_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL
stays at its 0x0000FFFF reset and all four PMA lane-invert bits stay clear.
`phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-reset-sequence` says so in its code comment:
"Still missing for actual video, named rather than implied: the DP lane map at
0x06C06C24 (0x00003210 in the capture, 0xFFFF at reset)".

Why it matters, measured
------------------------

Without the inverts the sink escalates the voltage swing 1 -> 2 -> 3 and never
reaches clock recovery. That was measured on the 8 GiB board on 2026-08-18.

Every trained link so far was trained by something that wrote these two
registers outside the driver: test instrumentation, or a script through devmem.
A link-training patch that does not move them onto the production path would
train nothing on a delivery image.

Where the values come from
--------------------------

Silicon, both of them, read off a live four-lane vendor link on the 8 GiB
board:

  lane_invert = <1 1 1 1>  -> the four per-lane PMA words 0xF000/0xF100/0xF200/
                              0xF300 (bytes 0x06C9E000/200/400/600) each read
                              0x0100, i.e. bit8 set
  lane_remap  = <0 1 2 3>  -> COMB0_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL reads 0x00003210, the
                              identity. Reset is 0x0000FFFF, so this is not a
                              value that is already there.

Both were re-read with the plug turned 180 degrees on 2026-08-19: same map,
same inverts, four lanes trained, picture confirmed by eye. So there is no
per-orientation table here and none should be added -- the flip is carried by
LINK_CTRL0 bit12 TYPEC_CONN_DIR alone.

What the vendor does and what this does
---------------------------------------

  - The vendor writes both from its DP phy's power_on, a path this tree does
    not have. This driver writes them from the Type-C mux callback, the only
    entry point from which a DP register write is reachable -- so a port that
    never enters DP alt mode never touches either register.
  - combo0_dp_lane_remap() carries a mirrored packing for a reversed plug and
    its orientation-aware call is commented out; the live register says the
    identity is correct either way round. This driver does not carry that
    branch.
  - The vendor does not put the USB values back. This driver snapshots them on
    the first DP entry and restores them when the mux takes the lanes away.

Ordering
--------

The board data goes down before the reset staircase of
`phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-reset-sequence`, the order used on every run
that produced a trained link (lane setup, then typec_mux_set(), then
phy_configure()). On the way out it is the other way round: teardown first, so
the link is back in reset before the values are reverted.

Hardware result, the 8 GiB board, 2026-08-19
--------------------------------------------

Item 1 below is settled. The combo-PHY's own `state` file reported that the
test instrumentation had not been used since boot, so nothing but the mux
callback can have written them:

    lane map    : 0x00003210   at 0x06C06C24   (the reset value is 0xFFFF)
    lane invert : 0xf          (bit n -> bit8 of PMA word 0xF000 + n*0x100)
    rate table  : 0x51D951D9   at 0x06C98020   (`phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-bracket-the-dp-rate-table` in place)

The map and the inverts reach the production path from the Type-C mux
callback.

This settles this patch and nothing else. `phy-allwinner-a733-combophy-dp-swing-and-pre-emphasis`
and `drm-a733-dp-link-training` rode the same kernel and are not proven by it
-- see their own headers. Items 2 and 3 below are still open: neither the
SuperSpeed negative control nor the restore-on-unplug was exercised in that
session.

Checks
------

  1. Done, see above: with a DP sink on J4 and alt mode entered,
     `devmem 0x06C06C24 32` reads 0x00003210 and `devmem 0x06C9E000 32` reads
     0x01000100, the PMA mirroring its 16-bit words into both halves, likewise
     0x06C9E200 / 0x06C9E400 / 0x06C9E600. Fails if: 0x0000FFFF or 0x00000000
     respectively.
  2. The negative control, which is the half that matters: with no sink
     attached, the same four addresses keep their USB values and `lsusb -t`
     still shows a SuperSpeed device at 10000M. RST_BUS_SERDES is shared and
     this is the driver that owns COMB0.
     Fails if: the DP values appear on a port that never entered DP alt mode,
     or SuperSpeed drops below 10000M.
  3. Restore: after an unplug, the four PMA words read what they read before
     the DP entry.
     Fails if: 0x0100 persists after the lanes go back to USB.

Hardware-proven for its own effect (item 1, the 8 GiB board, 2026-08-19);
items 2 and 3 still open. Builds clean at W=1; checkpatch 0/0.

Assisted-by: Claude

diff --git a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
--- a/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/allwinner/phy-sun60i-a733-combophy.c
@@ -54,6 +54,11 @@
  */
 #define  DP_RAWS_TXDW_CONV_4LANE	(DP_PHY_CFG_DATA_EN | DP_PHY_CFG_LN_EN | \
 					 DP_PHY_CFG_LN_RSTN)
+/* COMB0_PHY_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL (0x06C06C24) -- four 4-bit fields, one per DP
+ * lane, physical -> logical. Reset default 0xFFFF; this board's
+ * lane_remap = <0 1 2 3> is the identity 0x00003210.
+ */
+#define COMB0_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL		0x0C24
 #define USB3P1_PIPE_CLK_MAP_CTRL	0x0100
 #define USB3P1_PIPE_RXD_MAP_CTRL	0x0104
 #define  USB3P1_PIPE_MAP_MASK		GENMASK(3, 0)
@@ -118,6 +123,34 @@
 #define PMA_NUDGE_OFF			(0xC008 << 1)
 #define  PMA_NUDGE_CLR			(0xF << 8)
 
+/*
+ * Per-lane DP config word in the PMA; bit8 inverts the lane. Vendor
+ * combo0_dp_lane_invert() walks word index 0xF000 + n * 0x100. NOTE this is
+ * a BYTE offset, like PMA_NUDGE_OFF above and unlike PMA_DP_LANE_CFG below,
+ * which is a raw word index shifted at its call site -- the file carries both
+ * conventions, so the names say which.
+ */
+#define A733_DP_LANES			4
+#define PMA_DP_LANE_INV_OFF(n)		((0xF000 + (n) * 0x100) << 1)
+#define  PMA_DP_LANE_INV_EN		BIT(8)
+
+/*
+ * The two pieces of DP board data, both read off silicon with a live
+ * four-lane vendor link on the 8 GiB board and both confirmed identical with
+ * the plug turned 180 degrees:
+ *
+ *   lane_invert = <1 1 1 1> -> bit8 set in each of the four per-lane PMA words
+ *                              0xF000/0xF100/0xF200/0xF300.
+ *   lane_remap  = <0 1 2 3> -> COMB0_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL = 0x00003210, the
+ *                              identity. Reset is 0x0000FFFF, which is not it.
+ *
+ * There is NO per-orientation table here and a driver must not grow one: the
+ * flip is carried by LINK_CTRL0 bit12 TYPEC_CONN_DIR alone, and both values
+ * above are the same either way round.
+ */
+#define A733_DP_LANE_INVERT_DEFAULT	GENMASK(A733_DP_LANES - 1, 0)
+#define A733_DP_LANE_MAP_IDENTITY	0x00003210
+
 #define SERDES_REFCLK_RATE		100000000	/* serdes-phy-cfg = 100 MHz */
 #define PHY_LOCK_TIMEOUT_US		2000
 #define PMA_READY_TIMEOUT_US		10000
@@ -167,6 +200,16 @@ struct a733_combophy {
 	 * a board that never enters DP alt mode never executes any of them.
 	 */
 	bool			dp_active;
+	/* The DP lane map and lane inverts, and the USB values they displace.
+	 * Written when the mux hands the lanes to DisplayPort and put back when
+	 * it takes them away, so a port that never enters DP alt mode never
+	 * sees either register.
+	 */
+	u32			dp_lane_map;
+	u32			dp_lane_invert;
+	bool			dp_lanes_saved;
+	u32			saved_lane_map;
+	u16			saved_lane_cfg[A733_DP_LANES];
 	bool			inited;
 };
 
@@ -1459,6 +1502,79 @@ static void a733_combophy_sw_unregister(void *data)
 	typec_switch_unregister(data);
 }
 
+/* Vendor combo0_dp_lane_invert(): read-modify-write bit8 of each lane's PMA
+ * config word. Not orientation-dependent there and not here.
+ */
+static void a733_dp_lane_invert(struct a733_combophy *cp, u32 mask)
+{
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < A733_DP_LANES; i++) {
+		void __iomem *reg = cp->pma + PMA_DP_LANE_INV_OFF(i);
+		u16 v = readw(reg);
+
+		v &= ~PMA_DP_LANE_INV_EN;
+		if (mask & BIT(i))
+			v |= PMA_DP_LANE_INV_EN;
+		writew(v, reg);
+	}
+}
+
+/* Vendor combo0_dp_lane_remap(): nibble n carries lane n. That function has a
+ * mirrored packing for a reversed plug, but its only live caller passes
+ * TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NONE and the orientation-aware call is commented out -- and
+ * silicon agrees, the register reads the identity with the plug reversed.
+ *
+ * Not to be confused with the DisplayPort core's OWN lane remap,
+ * LANE_REMAP_CONTROL at 0x0574002C (UM 15.4.7.10): bit8 REMAP_ENABLE, [7:0] the
+ * four 2-bit mappings, [19:16] four per-lane inverts. That register is a
+ * different piece of hardware one block further down the pipe, its reset value
+ * is 0 (remap disabled, no inversion), and nothing here writes it. Two registers
+ * with the same job in the same link is exactly the pair a reader mixes up.
+ */
+static void a733_dp_lane_map(struct a733_combophy *cp, u32 map)
+{
+	writel(map, cp->top2 + COMB0_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL);
+}
+
+/*
+ * Hand the lanes their DisplayPort wiring, snapshotting the USB values on the
+ * first entry so leaving DP puts back what it displaced.
+ *
+ * Both callers hold cp->lock. The order is the one that is HW-proven: the board
+ * data goes down BEFORE the DP reset staircase runs, which is how a trained
+ * four-lane link was first reached on the 8 GiB board.
+ */
+static void a733_combophy_dp_lanes_enter(struct a733_combophy *cp)
+{
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	if (!cp->dp_lanes_saved) {
+		cp->saved_lane_map = readl(cp->top2 + COMB0_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL);
+		for (i = 0; i < A733_DP_LANES; i++)
+			cp->saved_lane_cfg[i] = readw(cp->pma +
+						      PMA_DP_LANE_INV_OFF(i));
+		cp->dp_lanes_saved = true;
+	}
+
+	a733_dp_lane_map(cp, cp->dp_lane_map);
+	a733_dp_lane_invert(cp, cp->dp_lane_invert);
+}
+
+static void a733_combophy_dp_lanes_leave(struct a733_combophy *cp)
+{
+	unsigned int i;
+
+	if (!cp->dp_lanes_saved)
+		return;
+
+	writel(cp->saved_lane_map, cp->top2 + COMB0_RAWS_TXD_MAP_CTRL);
+	for (i = 0; i < A733_DP_LANES; i++)
+		writew(cp->saved_lane_cfg[i], cp->pma + PMA_DP_LANE_INV_OFF(i));
+
+	cp->dp_lanes_saved = false;
+}
+
 /* COMB0 carries either SuperSpeed or DP, never both, and the lane routing lives
  * inside this PHY -- there is no external mux on this board. So the DisplayPort
  * alt-mode driver reaches the lanes through here, and this callback is the only
@@ -1474,10 +1590,13 @@ static void a733_combophy_sw_unregister(void *data)
  * capture of that state, and guessing it against a HW-proven 10 Gbps link is the
  * trade this tree does not make.
  *
- * Still missing for actual video, named rather than implied: the DP lane map at
- * 0x06C06C24 (0x00003210 in the capture, 0xFFFF at reset), the DP AUX/HPD front
- * end at 0x06C01E00 (0x03331131 in the capture, 0x00330000 at reset), and the PMA
- * link-rate registers. This is the reset and link-control sequence only.
+ * The DP lane map at 0x06C06C24 and the four PMA lane inverts are written from
+ * here. Measured consequence of missing inverts: the sink escalates the
+ * voltage swing 1 -> 2 -> 3 and never reaches clock recovery.
+ *
+ * Still missing for actual video, named rather than implied: the DP AUX/HPD
+ * front end at 0x06C01E00 (0x03331131 in the capture, 0x00330000 at reset),
+ * which belongs to the separate AUX/HPD PHY, and the swing/pre-emphasis tables.
  *
  * Returning 0 rather than an error stays deliberate: an error aborts the
  * alt-mode entry, and then nothing is learned about what the sink offers.
@@ -1495,6 +1614,10 @@ static int a733_combophy_typec_mux_set(struct typec_mux_dev *mux,
 	if (mode == TYPEC_STATE_SAFE || mode == TYPEC_STATE_USB) {
 		if (cp->dp_active) {
 			a733_combophy_dp_teardown(cp);
+			/* After the teardown, so the link is back in reset
+			 * before the board data is reverted.
+			 */
+			a733_combophy_dp_lanes_leave(cp);
 			cp->dp_active = false;
 			dev_info(cp->dev,
 				 "DP alt mode left, COMB0 links back in reset; SuperSpeed does not return without a phy_exit()/phy_init() cycle\n");
@@ -1536,6 +1659,7 @@ static int a733_combophy_typec_mux_set(struct typec_mux_dev *mux,
 		 "DP alt mode pin assignment %c: handing all four COMB0 lanes to DisplayPort\n",
 		 pin);
 	cp->dp_active = true;
+	a733_combophy_dp_lanes_enter(cp);
 	if (a733_combophy_dp_reset_seq(cp))
 		dev_err(cp->dev,
 			"DP link bring-up did not complete, see the handshake errors above\n");
@@ -1583,6 +1707,11 @@ static int a733_combophy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (!cp)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	cp->dev = dev;
+	/* Board data, not a policy: both values were read off a live vendor DP
+	 * link on this board and are the same in either plug orientation.
+	 */
+	cp->dp_lane_map = A733_DP_LANE_MAP_IDENTITY;
+	cp->dp_lane_invert = A733_DP_LANE_INVERT_DEFAULT;
 	mutex_init(&cp->lock);
 	cp->orientation = TYPEC_ORIENTATION_NORMAL;
 
